Goal
Prepare the team for the TMCC AI security engagement by completing key outreach, research, and planning before delivery begins.
Pre-Engagement Actions
Client communication
• Send Parisha the document request list next week, after it is reviewed and tightened.
• At kickoff, confirm the preferred day and time for regular weekly status calls.
• Ask Parisha to add a TMNA representative to the kickoff.
• Add a TMNA GRC/governance discussion to the meeting request list.
Stakeholder outreach
• Contact David Yu to request the Mandiant team point of contact.
• Context: Mandiant is supporting AI architecture-pattern work for TMCC.
• Request a meeting for next week.
• CC Stas, Adam, and Rashi; keep Rashi optional for attendance.
Research Work
AI security architecture patterns
• Start with the AI architecture-pattern topics listed in the SOW.
• Research MCP, AI agents, agentic identity and access management, and relevant security practices.
• Work with Smash on the research.
• Use findings to prepare for reviewing TMCC documentation and discussions with Mandiant.
AI discovery and protection
• Research how AI discovery/protection tools operate in practice, beyond vendor marketing.
• Use Salt as an initial example.
• Do initial research before involving Neil, the Salt/API security SME.
Governance and policy alignment
• Plan calls with both TMNA governance and TMCC governance teams.
• Understand TMNA’s parent-level AI security policies.
• Compare them with TMCC’s needs and identify policy gaps.
AI/MCP Gateway Vendor Evaluation
Criteria
• Moksh and Gauri should develop selection criteria and a scoring framework.
• Separate must-have from good-to-have capabilities.
• Ask them to share templates from prior engagements.
• Validate the criteria with the client before finalizing.
Vendor research
• Identify up to 10 AI/MCP gateway vendors.
• Begin outreach for demos and solution walkthroughs.
• Use the agreed criteria to assess vendors.
• Produce a scored summary after research and vendor discussions.
Immediate Deliverable
• Create a spreadsheet separating:
• pre-engagement research and planning tasks;
• tasks that begin once the engagement starts;
• owners and dependencies.
